# Kitchen Sink: Card Embedding Syntax

## Inline `:card` (atom format)

Mention a person: :card[Jamie]{id=0}

Mention a task: :card[Deploy]{id=2}

Multiple inline: :card[Jamie]{id=0} assigned :card[Deploy]{id=2} to :card[Sarah]{id=1}

## Block `::card` (embedded format)

### Person Cards

::card{id=0 format=embedded}

::card{id=1 format=embedded}

### Task Cards

::card{id=2 format=embedded}

::card{id=3 format=embedded}

## Block with explicit formats

### Atom format (inline-block)

::card{id=0 format=atom}

::card{id=2 format=atom}

### Fitted format

::card{id=0 format=fitted}

::card{id=2 format=fitted}

## Container `:::card` (isolated format)

:::card{id=0 format=isolated}
:::

:::card{id=2 format=isolated}
:::

## Mixed usage in context

> :card[Jamie]{id=0} said: "Let's ship :card[Deploy]{id=2} today!"

| Person | Task | Status |
|--------|------|--------|
| :card[Jamie]{id=0} | :card[Deploy]{id=2} | In Progress |
| :card[Sarah]{id=1} | :card[Tests]{id=3} | Todo |
